{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects","id":17385,"title":"Pacts and Merit-Related Cover Aspects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-24T16:56:19-08:00","id":17385,"title":"Pacts and Merit-Related Cover Aspects","content":"The section on Pacts says that it is possible to make deals for aspects of a given person's life. What if that aspect is represented by a Merit? Does the demon then get that Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T17:11:52-08:00","id":17389,"title":"","content":"Yes I think that is part of the whole point. For instance you can by a homeless man's connection to his parents in exchange for the Resource dots to allow him to live in a fancy condo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T18:58:26-08:00","id":17442,"title":"","content":"I believe what OP is trying to say is could I say, bargain away a rich man's life experiences as being rich and gain Resource Merit for my Demon character, and in general the answer to that is no. It might be trickier with something like Mentor or True Friend though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T19:45:01-08:00","id":17459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=17442#post17442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe what OP is trying to say is could I say, bargain away a rich man's life experiences as being rich and gain Resource Merit for my Demon character, and in general the answer to that is no. It might be trickier with something like Mentor or True Friend though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Honestly, if we'd included an explanation of how pacts relate to every single Merit, some of them would be things you can bargain for. As is, you can bargain for a relationship that's embodied by a Merit, but by default, you don't get the special mechanical benefits of that Merit. The ST ruling otherwise is really easy and doesn't break anything, though.<br /> <br /> Usually, I don't actually give NPCs full complements of Merits, so I wouldn't usually give one a Mentor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T09:38:17-08:00","id":17762,"title":"","content":"A possible hose rule I've been considering is allowing pacts to give the Demon Merits, but incuring XP debt for them. That way you don't have weird situations like bargaining for someone's True Friend and not getting the benefits of one, or trading for the soul of a Giant person but not actually having the benefits of being Giant in that cover. But you also don't effectively get free XP out of contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T18:34:46-08:00","id":18072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=17762#post17762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possible hose rule I've been considering is allowing pacts to give the Demon Merits, but incuring XP debt for them. That way you don't have weird situations like bargaining for someone's True Friend and not getting the benefits of one, or trading for the soul of a Giant person but not actually having the benefits of being Giant in that cover. But you also don't effectively get free XP out of contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, if you don't mind a bit more bookkeeping, attach bargained for merits to specific Covers, and require that you have to be in the specified Cover to get the benefits of the merit. You could also be a bit more strict about rolling to maintain a cover if it's got a lot of merits on it too, if you feel like it's problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T19:53:28-08:00","id":18116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=18072#post18072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alternately, if you don't mind a bit more bookkeeping, attach bargained for merits to specific Covers, and require that you have to be in the specified Cover to get the benefits of the merit. You could also be a bit more strict about rolling to maintain a cover if it's got a lot of merits on it too, if you feel like it's problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, that's not how it works by default? I assumed you could have, say, one Cover with Giant Size, one with Small Framed, and one with Striking Looks 2, and those merits would not apply unless you were in the cover that has the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T22:22:21-08:00","id":18183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=18116#post18116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wait, that's not how it works by default? I assumed you could have, say, one Cover with Giant Size, one with Small Framed, and one with Striking Looks 2, and those merits would not apply unless you were in the cover that has the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The question arises with dots created by acquiring a cover or aspects thereof, rather than bought with Experiences striaght-up. I'm liking the XP debt idea myself. Or if the payer wants to stay flexible with their upcoming Experience spends, they can stick with relying on Legend to access the mechanical benefits of Merits from that bargain until they learn them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-26-2013, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T23:00:55-08:00","id":18199,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would give the benefit of &quot;most&quot; (read: determined on a case-by-case basis) Merits this way. But, of course, anything you haven't paid for with experience doesn't have the plot protection that regular Merits get. Eg. if you've bought True Friend with xp, you have a true friend for good, baring exceptional circumstances. And even if that friend get killed, or something, I'd refund you the merit points. If you stole someone elses True Friend through a pact, you would have to do something active to keep the relationship from deteriorating over time (which, in this particular instance might even put your Cover at risk).<br /> <br /> Sorta like the difference between buying dots in Resource and just robbing a bank. If that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T01:52:55-08:00","id":19045,"title":"","content":"I'd allow the demon to use cover XP to purchase cover-specific merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T07:55:19-08:00","id":19180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=19045#post19045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow the demon to use cover XP to purchase cover-specific merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T12:33:03-08:00","id":19858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/17385-pacts-and-merit-related-cover-aspects?p=19045#post19045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow the demon to use cover XP to purchase cover-specific merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was how I thought it worked... One thing I'm noticing about DtD the more its discussed is that a lot of things don't work the way I intuitively expect them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T14:57:01-08:00","id":20808,"title":"","content":"The notion of Cover-specific Merits purchased via Cover XP is a good one; but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s quite enough. It wouldn\u2019t, for instance, cover a man bargaining away his kingdom for a horse. <br /> <br /> I think I <i>would</i> allow a demon to include Assets on his side of the pact; but they\u2019d need to be Merits that the mortal has, the mortal would lose them, and they\u2019d become Cover-specific Merits for the demon. I\u2019d also consider ruling that Cover-specific Merits are capped by your Cover: as long as your Cover is 5 or more, this isn\u2019t a problem; but as it drops into the 1-to-4 range, his Cover-specific Merits start degrading or going offline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}